   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">Hi lavaan users,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">Does anyone know the syntax for fixing the residual variance of an item in bifactor CFA model to equal 0? I feel like this should be easy to find, but I&#39;m having trouble finding this info in previous posts/other places. </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">For example, if I wanted to fix the residual variance of item z2 below to 0--what would the syntax would be? </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">model &lt;- &#39;g =~x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 + x5 + z1 + z2 + z3 + z4 + z5 + z6</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">f1 =~ z1 + z2 + z3 + z4 + z5 + z6</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">f2 =~ x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 + x5&#39; <br>  <br>fit &lt;- lavaan::cfa(model, data = item.set2,  ordered = </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">c(&quot;x1&quot;, &quot;x2&quot;, &quot;x3&quot;, &quot;x4&quot;, &quot;x5&quot;, &quot;z1&quot;, &quot;z2&quot;, &quot;z3&quot;, &quot;z4&quot;, &quot;z5&quot;, &quot;z6&quot;),<br><a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423551457000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0rXhiKoYwJGV6bttSzBcmO\">std.lv</a> = TRUE, missing = &quot;pairwise&quot;, orthogonal = TRUE) <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">Thank you!</div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "X_JGxC5YAQAJ",
   "from": "nick judd",
